ntation`) is inferred from the strategy's statement that documentation is a separately owned work stream — verify with the actual docs team before scheduling.\n- **E001 component mapping** (non-obvious): the packaging format spans Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines content and is consumed by Dashboard code. Assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks` (tutorials are primarily notebook artifacts, and the format exists to keep them independent of Dashboard releases); the span is noted here per the component-name constraint.\n- **Scope trap — tutorial maintenance**: HLR-2 requires tutorials \"tested against the current release\" and the problem statement calls them \"maintained\" tutorials, but the strategy scopes no ongoing re-validation process for future releases and the out-of-scope list does not address it. Recurring per-release re-testing effort is unplanned; the validation manifest from the packaging format mitigates but does not eliminate it.\n- **Contribution process without tooling** (consistent, noted for awareness): the contribution process is documented (HLR-4) while submission tooling is explicitly out of scope — the docs must describe a process that has no tooling this release; flagged so the docs epic scopes it as process documentation only.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain timing (Dependencies table absent; no upstream/vendor gating identified). All epics proceed on the single plan above.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30123,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae412547b66845e7","agent_id":"a77f5419bda797510","session_id":"3e13a806-c285-42c0-9767-e97cfc099643","uuid":"c20d8242-4674-4a61-a7f8-7f1917d01eb8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:33:25.694Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
