{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-85f0ed0c-fe5d-41ae-a69b-1b836e12a877","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a15a08506ffea47c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-jo6iljpf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned and testable artifacts independent of Dashboard releases. It produces the format specification and the validation means for tutorial packages: the metadata that describes a tutorial, the pinning of the images a tutorial runs on, and a validation manifest against which a packaged tutorial can be mechanically checked.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the tutorial packaging format covering:\n  - Tutorial metadata (identity, journey description, kind: notebook-based or pipeline-based, and the fields a consuming UI needs to present and launch it)\n  - Pinned images: how the notebook/workbench image (and any other images the tutorial depends on) are pinned so a tutorial runs reproducibly\n  - Validation manifest: the machine-checkable description of what a packaged tutorial must satisfy to be considered valid and testable\n- Define format versioning so tutorial packages can evolve and be tested independently of Dashboard releases\n- Provide the validation means by which a tutorial package is checked against the format (validation manifest is passed/fail-checkable without a Dashboard release)\n- Ensure the format covers both tutorial kinds named by the strategy: notebook-based tutorials (launched by opening a workbench with the notebook) and pipeline-based tutorials (launched by importing the pipeline)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The packaging format specification defines tutorial metadata, image pinning, and a validation manifest, satisfying the 