and be tested independently of Dashboard releases\n42\t- Provide the validation means by which a tutorial package is checked against the format (validation manifest is passed/fail-checkable without a Dashboard release)\n43\t- Ensure the format covers both tutorial kinds named by the strategy: notebook-based tutorials (launched by opening a workbench with the notebook) and pipeline-based tutorials (launched by importing the pipeline)\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- The packaging format specification defines tutorial metadata, image pinning, and a validation manifest, satisfying the elements named in HLR-3.\n48\t- A tutorial packaged per the format can be validated mechanically by checking it against its validation manifest, with no Dashboard release involved in the check.\n49\t- The format carries a version, and a packaged tutorial declares the format version it targets, so tutorials are versioned independently of Dashboard releases.\n50\t- The format supports both a notebook-based tutorial and a pipeline-based tutorial (demonstrated by a minimal exemplar package of each kind that passes validation).\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — full coverage. The tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) is this epic's deliverable; tutorials become versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases.\n55\t- This epic also enables HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P0), which build on the format; priority is inherited as P0 accordingly.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-924c3c25530292cc","agent_id":"a1a52b8108f0b1d59","session_id":"3e13a806-c285-42c0-9767-e97cfc099643","uuid":"0cdc81e5-d282-405f-b737-144a341c91cb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:36:11.292Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2c63b4001a0e937","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
