ategy's problem statement\ndemands. No scope duplication: E001's minimal exemplar packages are validation fixtures, not a\nrebuild of E003/E004's curated tutorials. E003 (five authored tutorials) is a single-logical-change\nsweep over an enumerated journey set presented by the strategy as one work item (HLR-2), same team\nand packaging pattern — the compliant shape, but the Health Warnings section carries no concrete\nconditional re-split trigger for it (minor issue, recorded below; does not dock the criterion).\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nNo Investigation epics — appropriate, since the strategy's Open Questions section is \"None\" and no\nuncertainty changes downstream structure. All five epics are Implementation and each produces a\nconcrete artifact (format specification + validation means; gallery feature; tutorial packages;\ndocs topics). E005 correctly carries `implementation_type: docs-authoring` under type\nImplementation. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set, and none are needed (no gates).\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nAll five epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric); no epic mixes in\n`investigation_signals`. Signal values are consistent with the rationales and the strategy content:\nE001's `existing_foundation: -1` (greenfield format, no existing packaging machinery) contrasts\ncorrectly with E002/E003/E004's `1` (extension of existing GA surfaces); `open_questions: 1` across\nall epics matches the strategy's explicit \"None\"; `external_dependency: 1` matches the absence of\nany Dependencies table or vendor gating. Architecture-claims calibration checks out: E001-E004 score\n`architecture_claims: 1` with rationales citing `.context/architecture-context/.../notebooks.md`,\n`dashboard.md`, and `data-science-pipelines.md`, all of which exist; E005 scores `0` with a\nself-aware rationale (no architecture-context file covers the Documentation component, and the epic\ndocuments not-yet-built functionality), which is not a calibration miss under the rule. Computed\n`ai_implementability`/`ai_implementability_score` values were not checked per instructions.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLRs. Rule-mandated ACs are present where applicable:\nE005 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review-against-implementation AC and a docs-toolchain\nbuild-pass AC; no konflux-chain or replacement epics exist, so those mandates don't apply. No\nAC states an externally-controlled precondition — each AC conditions on the epic's own deliverable\n(e.g., E003's \"runs to completion when opened in a workbench... on the current release\" is a\nverification of the authored tutorial, not a granted availability). No epic body references sibling\nepics by bare draft ID.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nThe strategy's full scope is accounted for: gallery + launch mechanics (HLR-1 → E002, both launch\nmodes as separate ACs), all six tutorials with per-tutorial testing against the current release\n(HLR-2 → E003's five + E004's one, each with packaging/validation/testing ACs), packaging format\n(HLR-3 → E001, including versioning and both tutorial kinds), and documentation of both usage and\ncontribution process (HLR-4 → E005, with the out-of-scope submission tooling correctly scoped as\nprocess-only documentation). Out-of-scope items (community intake tooling, localization) are\nrespected. Strategy-level context is carried forward rather than dropped: missing strategy sections,\nteam inference, the E001 component-span note, the tutorial-maintenance scope trap, and the\ncontribution-process-without-tooling note are all recorded in Health Warnings and reflected in the\nrelevant epics. No conditional branches are needed (no bounded uncertain outcomes). Tiered Delivery\nN/A is justified — no external dependencies with uncertain timing.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25