{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afc8d7d1ead9e820","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into a project | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Author five notebook-based curated tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Author the first-pipeline curated tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document the tutorial gallery and the tutorial contribution process | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n21\t\n22\t## Dependency DAG\n23\t\n24\t```mermaid\n25\tgraph TD\n26\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 Tutorial packaging format] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 Dashboard gallery]\n27\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 Notebook tutorials]\n28\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 Pipeline tutorial]\n29\t    E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 Documentation]\n30\t    E002 --> E005\n31\t    E003 --> E005\n32\t    E004 --> E005\n33\t```\n34\t\n35\t## DAG Justification\n36\t\n37\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n38\t|------|------|-----------|\n39\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The Dashboard gallery code builds against the packaging format — it parses tutorial metadata and the validation manifest and uses pinned images to launch tutorials. The format/schema must exist before the consuming code is written. |\n40\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The notebook tutorials are packaged to the format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest); packaging cannot start before the format is defined. |\n41\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged to the same format. |\n42\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation epic is blocked by all Implementation epics. |\n43\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Docs describe the built gallery and launch mechanics. |\n44\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Docs describe the built tutorials and contribution process. |\n45\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Docs describe the built tutorials and contribution process. |\n46\t\n47\t**Parallel non-edges (deliberate):**\n48\t\n49\t- **E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004** — the gallery (Dashboard repo) and the tutorial content (notebook and pipeline artifacts) live in different repos/components with no shared build artifacts. The gallery consumes tutorials as *content* at runtime, not as a build-against artifact; per Rule 13's configuration/content distinction this coupling is expressed as an acceptance criterion on the gallery epic (\"launching a tutorial packaged in the defined format succeeds end-to-end, verified with at least one tutorial from the curated set or an equivalent fixture\"), never as a DAG edge. Edges here would serialize three independently staffed work streams.\n50\t- **E003 ∥ E004** — different components and teams (Notebooks/Workbenches vs. Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines); the tutorial split follows the component boundary, and the two content sets share only the packaging format contract, which E001 provides to both.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n53\t\n54\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic(s) | Notes |\n55\t|-----|----------|------------------------|---------|-------|\n56\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Tutorial gallery in the Dashboard; one-click launch into the user's project (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import) | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Direct mapping. |\n57\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Six curated tutorials covering the core journeys, each tested against the current release | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/team boundary: five notebook-based journeys (first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) → E003 (Notebooks/Workbenches); the first-pipeline journey → E004 (Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines). Both epics are P0; the HLR is fully covered only when both complete. |\n58\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Direct mapping. E001 maps to a P1 HLR but **inherits P0** via priority inheritance: HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P0) transitively depend on the format (Rule 13 edges above), and an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0. Not a priority inversion. |\n59\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process for new tutorials | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Direct mapping. Priority via the docs-authoring exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1), not inheritance from the P0 implementations. |\n60\t\n61\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. No redundant/overlapping HLR pairs were identified.\n62\t\n63\t## Health Warnings\n64\t\n65\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, no Non-Functional Requirements, and no Technical Approach / Staff Engineer Input. Decomposition proceeded from the HLR table, affected components list, and problem statement. Epic acceptance criteria were derived at the functional level of the HLRs.\n66\t- **Team inference**: owner teams were taken from `.context/architecture-context/` owning-team fields (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). No architecture-context file exists for the Documentation component; E005's team (`RHOAI Documentation`) is inferred from the strategy's statement that documentation is a separately owned work stream — verify with the actual docs team before scheduling.\n67\t- **E001 component mapping** (non-obvious): the packaging format spans Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines content and is consumed by Dashboard code. Assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks` (tutorials are primarily notebook artifacts, and the format exists to keep them independent of Dashboard releases); the span is noted here per the component-name constraint.\n68\t- **Scope trap — tutorial maintenance**: HLR-2 requires tutorials \"tested against the current release\" and the problem statement calls them \"maintained\" tutorials, but the strategy scopes no ongoing re-validation process for future releases and the out-of-scope list does not address it. Recurring per-release re-testing effort is unplanned; the validation manifest from the packaging format mitigates but does not eliminate it.\n69\t- **E003 size watch** (single epic, five tutorials): E003 authors five notebook-based tutorials in one epic. This is a single logical change — one mechanical sweep over the enumerated journey set the strategy presents as one work item (HLR-2), same team (Workbenches), same component (Notebooks), and the same packaging/validation/testing pattern per tutorial — so it is not split. Estimated effort: roughly 5 journeys × (authoring + packaging + test-against-current-release) per tutorial, on the order of one sprint for one author. **Conditional re-split trigger:** if combined authoring and testing is projected to exceed one sprint of effort (e.g., any single tutorial's authoring-plus-testing runs over ~2 days, or fewer than all five are within a sprint's reach at mid-sprint check-in), split E003 by journey into separate epics (new IDs continuing the sequence), keeping the packaging-format dependency and per-tutorial ACs intact in each.\n70\t- **Contribution process without tooling** (consistent, noted for awareness): the contribution process is documented (HLR-4) while submission tooling is explicitly out of scope — the docs must describe a process that has no tooling this release; flagged so the docs epic scopes it as process documentation only.\n71\t\n72\t## Tiered Delivery\n73\t\n74\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain timing (Dependencies table absent; no upstream/vendor gating identified). All epics proceed on the single plan above.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc7071994d4a775","agent_id":"aa0c961fcb2baa8eb","session_id":"3e13a806-c285-42c0-9767-e97cfc099643","uuid":"5d4d3ddb-d6d4-4869-8398-ecaf3e4206a2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:39:20.834Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afc8d7d1ead9e820","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
