{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7d9f5d0ffbe9f39","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: -1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned and testable artifacts independent of Dashboard releases. It produces the format specification and the validation means for tutorial packages: the metadata that describes a tutorial, the pinning of the images a tutorial runs on, and a validation manifest against which a packaged tutorial can be mechanically checked.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define the tutorial packaging format covering:\n38\t  - Tutorial metadata (identity, journey description, kind: notebook-based or pipeline-based, and the fields a consuming UI needs to present and launch it)\n39\t  - Pinned images: how the notebook/workbench image (and any other images the tutorial depends on) are pinned so a tutorial runs reproducibly\n40\t  - Validation manifest: the machine-checkable description of what a packaged tutorial must satisfy to be considered valid and testable\n41\t- Define format versioning so tutorial packages can evolve and be tested independently of Dashboard releases\n42\t- Provide the validation means by which a tutorial package is checked against the format (validation manifest is passed/fail-checkable without a Dashboard release)\n43\t- Ensure the format covers both tutorial kinds named by the strategy: notebook-based tutorials (launched by opening a workbench with the notebook) and pipeline-based tutorials (launched by importing the pipeline)\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- The packaging format specification defines tutorial metadata, image pinning, and a validation manifest, satisfying the elements named in HLR-3.\n48\t- A tutorial packaged per the format can be validated mechanically by checking it against its validation manifest, with no Dashboard release involved in the check.\n49\t- The format carries a version, and a packaged tutorial declares the format version it targets, so tutorials are versioned independently of Dashboard releases.\n50\t- The format supports both a notebook-based tutorial and a pipeline-based tutorial (demonstrated by a minimal exemplar package of each kind that passes validation).\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** — full coverage. The tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) is this epic's deliverable; tutorials become versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases.\n55\t- This epic also enables HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P0), which build on the format; priority is inherited as P0 accordingly.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc7071994d4a775","agent_id":"aa0c961fcb2baa8eb","session_id":"3e13a806-c285-42c0-9767-e97cfc099643","uuid":"e8944f9c-c292-4e13-bd88-e9e95dcba4fc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:39:23.379Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7d9f5d0ffbe9f39","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
